A||||9||hugh||Need to Identify a Fiero.||||1||
Z||000000||hugh||12-21-2000||09:12 PM||||There is a white notch back with 4 flats sitting inside a fenced yard at a repair shop near my house.It has apparently been sitting for quite some time and I can buy it without a title for about $300 or maybe less.I was told it is a 4 speed,4 cylinder.It has a wing.It is supposed to run,but who knows?My question is this,How do I tell what year and model it is if it has no emblems(I will probably get to see it this weekend)and would it be worth getting ? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||12-21-2000||09:25 PM||||check tail lights it has the year on them<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||12-21-2000||09:25 PM||||I know I may sound like a retard, but you can check the VIN.  You should be able to find it somewhere.  Archie started a post on where the numbers are, but I don't know where it is.  If the VINs are missing, it may be stolen.  With the no title and everything.  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-21-2000||09:34 PM||||A 4cyl. 4-sp. must be an '84, since they went to a 5-sp. in '85.<P>Look at the VIN and it will confirm this.....look at the 10th digit, if it's an E it's an '84, F is '85, G is '86, H is '87 and J is '88.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||12-21-2000||09:34 PM||||If the rear decklid is kind of funky looking with a large grill in the middle and solid panels on the sides, it is an 84. Another clue is the 4cyl/4speed, wasn't that only in 84? I usually don't give much more than $200 for a parts car, but if it is in good shape it may be worth more. If the tranny is a m19 (4.10 final drive) some folks might like to have it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||12-21-2000||09:40 PM||||I found the post:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004468.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004468.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||V8Fiero||12-22-2000||01:48 AM||||Um.... Open up the drivers side door and see when the manufacture date was.  That tell it all..................||||reg||1
Z||000007||hugh||12-22-2000||04:45 PM||||Thanks,I went today and looked .It was snow covered,I was cold so I didn't see much,except the interior is rough.The car has been advertised in the papers as required by law to sell it without the title.It is supposed to run,but needs a clutch.It can be bought for $400.If anyone in my area is interested I will get a phone number for you. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||12-22-2000||05:16 PM||||Personally, I'd never buy another car without a title. Can't even take the remains to the crusher anymore without a title. All modern cars have a title...it's usually just that the seller is not the "legal" owner. In this case, it might be abandoned or a "mechanic's lien" because the owner never coughed up the cash on a repair job. On the other hand, it might be stolen. A non-running 84 with a trashed interior and a bad clutch is NOT worth $400 in my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000009||hugh||12-22-2000||05:44 PM||||It's not worth much to me either.It is legal though in NJ to sell a vehicle for an unpaid bill or an unclaimed car after certain requirements are met.My reputation is more valuable to me than anything else,so I would not jeopardize it for something as trivial as a car,even a Fiero.||||reg||1
